1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,910
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,310
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:06,380
(Episode 15)

4
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,510
Su Ah.

5
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:10,320
Wake up and get ready
for kindergarten.

6
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,050
You're going to be late.

7
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,150
- Yes, Great-Grandma.
- Okay.

8
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:21,290
Why did you have to stop her
on her way to work to scold her?

9
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:24,060
She was crying, all right?

10
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:25,900
You know how good my eyes are.

11
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,130
Oh, come on.

12
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,940
Mrs. Choi helped you out,
so why are you acting like this?

13
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:33,810
Just stay quiet and do nothing.

14
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:40,150
What did you two talk about
with Da Mi yesterday?

15
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:43,310
- Something happened, right?
- Why do you ask?

16
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:45,380
Nothing happened.

17
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:48,020
Then why were her eyes so swollen?

18
00:00:49,490 --> 00:00:50,890
I'm certain she was crying.

19
00:00:51,890 --> 00:00:53,530
I'm telling you, Da Mi was crying.

20
00:00:55,790 --> 00:00:57,130
Nothing gets past you.

21
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,200
Absolutely nothing.

22
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:02,800
Did you make your little sister cry?

23
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:12,710
Goodness. I think he did.

24
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,010
That's unusual.

25
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:18,050
When he was young,
he used to cherish her so much.

26
00:01:23,490 --> 00:01:24,560
Thank you.

27
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:29,260
(K Department Store)

28
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:33,570
Did you see the customer out safely?

29
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:36,470
Yes. The sales target
for this month is high,

30
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:38,100
so I was secretly worried,

31
00:01:38,170 --> 00:01:39,870
but I think we are off
to a good start.

32
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,110
The customer really liked it.

33
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:45,840
Setting aside those suit pants
for her earlier...

34
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,410
was a really smart move, Min Hee.

35
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:48,680
Great job.

36
00:01:48,950 --> 00:01:49,950
Really?

37
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:53,080
She always seemed to choose
dresses in the past,

38
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:55,420
but considering the atmosphere
of her upcoming event,

39
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:58,160
I thought that would
suit her better.

40
00:01:58,890 --> 00:02:01,490
I'm so relieved
that she chose it in the end.

41
00:02:01,630 --> 00:02:03,830
I was so nervous
we wouldn't make a sale today.

42
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:06,300
You feel a lot of pressure
when making sales, right?

43
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:07,670
I do,

44
00:02:07,730 --> 00:02:10,130
but it comes back as an incentive,
so it's fine.

45
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,500
When I get my bonus this month,

46
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:13,870
I think I can pay
for my brother's tuition...

47
00:02:13,870 --> 00:02:15,740
without taking out a loan.

48
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:18,480
How many semesters
did you say he has left?

49
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:20,380
He's starting the first semester
of his third year.

50
00:02:21,310 --> 00:02:25,120
- He still has quite a way to go.
- Still, I'm happy that I can...

51
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:26,350
support him.

52
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:28,250
Right.

53
00:02:28,990 --> 00:02:30,790
Min Hee,
I will organize the hangers,

54
00:02:30,790 --> 00:02:32,360
so please clear this table.

55
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:33,960
Okay.

56
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:41,600
Gosh.

57
00:02:43,270 --> 00:02:44,840
Since when was this here?

58
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:49,610
Where did you find that tablet?

59
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:52,240
I think it was stuck
between the chairs here.

60
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:55,280
It was pushed in so deep
that we didn't notice it.

61
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:56,650
I wonder whose it is...

62
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:57,920
Let me see it.

63
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:01,820
(Unlock pattern)

64
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,520
See?

65
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:07,960
The pattern is exactly
the same as yours.

66
00:03:08,930 --> 00:03:11,000
Look, I am not lying.

67
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:14,030
You're right.
It's the exact same model, too.

68
00:03:15,230 --> 00:03:17,900
It belongs to that customer
from before.

69
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,310
Is it someone you know?

70
00:03:21,110 --> 00:03:22,670
Min Hee, do you remember...

71
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:25,740
that customer who spent a fortune
on her brother's card?

72
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:28,610
Yes, of course I remember.

73
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,580
Since we delivered her purchases,

74
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:32,180
we should still have
her contact information.

75
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:33,420
Could you check on that for me?

76
00:03:33,890 --> 00:03:35,020
Yes, I will do that.

77
00:03:45,530 --> 00:03:46,630
The customer you are calling
is unavailable.

78
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:48,600
Please leave a message
after the tone.

79
00:03:54,470 --> 00:03:55,610
The customer you are calling
is unavailable.

80
00:03:55,670 --> 00:03:58,610
Please leave a message
after the tone.

81
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:03,480
How am I supposed to return this?

82
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:06,850
I need to find my tablet too.

83
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,330
How dare they summon my person...

84
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,160
to their company?

85
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:25,270
They don't even realize
it will only hurt them in the end.

86
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:32,810
I hope they don't get
completely wiped out by Dr. Ju.

87
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:42,250
The reason I asked
to see you like this...

88
00:04:42,350 --> 00:04:45,820
It must be regarding
Madam Chairwoman's health, right?

89
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:47,730
That's correct.

90
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:52,800
My wife doesn't show it,
but she's incredibly worried.

91
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:59,940
Since our family is not exactly
an ordinary family,

92
00:05:00,610 --> 00:05:02,610
when it comes to my mother's health,

93
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:05,110
it's true that we can't afford
to let our guard down.

94
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:08,750
But seeing my mother rely solely
on you, Dr. Ju,

95
00:05:08,750 --> 00:05:10,650
for all her treatments
and consultations...

96
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:12,520
Are you saying you want her...

97
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,890
to get outpatient treatment
at a university hospital?

98
00:05:14,950 --> 00:05:16,550
(Hwanggeum Capital)

99
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,520
As expected of you, Dr. Ju...

100
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,430
Yes, that is correct.

101
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Currently,
Madam Chairwoman's health...

102
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:28,800
has far more clear days
than cloudy ones.

103
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:30,870
And when her mind is clear,

104
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:33,440
she fully grasps
the overall management...

105
00:05:33,710 --> 00:05:36,210
of both Hwanggeum Capital
and Hwanggeum Apparel,

106
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:37,410
along with their performance,

107
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:40,680
and flawlessly reviews the plans
for the next 1, 3, 5,

108
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,710
and even ten years.

109
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:44,750
There are absolutely
no abnormalities...

110
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:46,050
in her other vital signs, either.

111
00:05:47,590 --> 00:05:51,420
But most importantly,
it's Madam Chairwoman's own decision.

112
00:05:51,690 --> 00:05:53,090
So, for the time being,

113
00:05:54,530 --> 00:05:56,390
are you saying it's fine...

114
00:05:56,460 --> 00:06:00,130
to continue leaving
my mother in your care, Dr. Ju?

115
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,970
Yes, that is correct.

116
00:06:08,610 --> 00:06:10,740
If you are finished,
I will take my leave.

117
00:06:11,510 --> 00:06:12,710
Wait a moment, Dr. Ju.

118
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:17,450
When and how did you
first cross paths...

119
00:06:17,650 --> 00:06:19,420
with my mother?

120
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,760
I'm asking
because I'm genuinely curious.

121
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:27,230
Even when I ask her,
she absolutely refuses to tell me.

122
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:33,130
If Madam Chairwoman hasn't
told you herself,

123
00:06:33,330 --> 00:06:35,330
there must be a good reason for it.

124
00:06:35,670 --> 00:06:36,900
How could I possibly dare...

125
00:06:36,930 --> 00:06:39,170
speak on her behalf
and tell you myself?

126
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:42,070
I will take my leave now.

127
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:45,180
(Hwanggeum Capital)

128
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:58,290
What a loyal dog.

129
00:06:59,690 --> 00:07:01,430
So what if he is a doctor?

130
00:07:01,890 --> 00:07:03,060
Give me a break.

131
00:07:03,630 --> 00:07:05,330
It's nothing to worry about.

132
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:08,930
But...

133
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:14,070
Just how much money is my mother
paying him to do this?

134
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,650
(Traffic Accident Report
and Summary)

135
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:24,880
You had to go there for nothing,
all because of me, Dr. Ju.

136
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:27,190
What did he say?

137
00:07:29,690 --> 00:07:31,790
Understood. You may go back to work.

138
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:39,700
It's a tangled mess right now,
but just you wait.

139
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:42,130
I will eventually...

140
00:07:42,870 --> 00:07:45,500
find the missing clue.

141
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:54,450
(K Department Store)

142
00:07:57,850 --> 00:07:59,150
All of this?

143
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,550
Yes, I would like a refund.

144
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:02,850
But...

145
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:05,560
I returned the packages
sent to my house,

146
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,760
so they should arrive by tomorrow.

147
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:09,530
(K Department Store)

148
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:12,930
Is that not possible?

149
00:08:13,730 --> 00:08:14,970
The purchase was originally made
with a card...

150
00:08:14,970 --> 00:08:15,970
under someone else's name.

151
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:18,440
Our manager went through
the verification process...

152
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:19,740
at the time of purchase.

153
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:23,370
You were also here
to confirm it yourself.

154
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:27,180
Hello, sir.
I can help you with that.

155
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:35,490
The returned packages
have been confirmed.

156
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:38,820
The items you took with you that day
have also been verified.

157
00:08:39,190 --> 00:08:40,760
Thank you.

158
00:08:41,290 --> 00:08:44,400
However, there are a few
items missing.

159
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:49,000
Min Hee, have the items we sent
for alterations come back yet?

160
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,140
- Just a moment.
- Okay.

161
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:56,870
They're still processing them.
They must be backed up.

162
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:02,510
They're not answering.

163
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:07,850
- Excuse me...
- Yes, sir.

164
00:09:07,990 --> 00:09:10,450
Then just leave out
the altered items...

165
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:13,930
If you ever do this again,

166
00:09:14,190 --> 00:09:17,660
I will not ask any questions.

167
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,900
I will kick you both out
of this house.

168
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,900
I can't stand the sight of you.
Get out.

169
00:09:27,410 --> 00:09:29,770
Sir, you seem to be in a hurry,

170
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,680
but would you like
to have a seat and wait?

171
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,440
Pardon?

172
00:09:36,710 --> 00:09:38,050
Are you going there yourself?

173
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:48,760
Please...

174
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,960
just wait a moment.

175
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,090
Hello. By any chance,

176
00:10:23,330 --> 00:10:25,530
has order M89001 been processed?

177
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:37,980
(K Department Store)

178
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:40,910
That was fast, right?

179
00:10:43,950 --> 00:10:45,850
Here, Da Mi. Drink some water first.

180
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:47,590
Thank you.

181
00:10:58,030 --> 00:10:59,030
Thanks.

182
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,240
You didn't have to go
through all this trouble.

183
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:12,940
I have to do what I can.
It's what you wanted, right?

184
00:11:15,210 --> 00:11:19,180
Your refund has been processed, sir.
Here is your full receipt.

185
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,390
Yes, thank you.

186
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:24,520
Right.

187
00:11:25,990 --> 00:11:28,360
Your sister left her tablet behind.

188
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:30,460
I called her, but she didn't answer,

189
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:32,700
so I would appreciate it
if you could give it to her.

190
00:11:32,930 --> 00:11:34,130
You're saying this is my sister's?

191
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,830
I don't think
she even knows she had lost it.

192
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:40,670
My sister is a bit
eccentric and clumsy,

193
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:41,970
as you probably noticed.

194
00:11:42,110 --> 00:11:43,440
Being eccentric...

195
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,540
means she has a creative side,

196
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:46,980
and being clumsy...

197
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,880
means that in at least
one specific area,

198
00:11:48,950 --> 00:11:51,180
she has strong focus.

199
00:11:52,250 --> 00:11:55,150
She seemed like someone who shines
like the hot summer sun.

200
00:11:55,850 --> 00:11:58,090
Did she seem that way?
That's surprising.

201
00:11:58,490 --> 00:12:00,320
Anyway, I will make sure
to give it to her.

202
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:01,990
Have a good day.

203
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:08,670
Thank you. Take care.

204
00:12:13,470 --> 00:12:15,770
And here I was,
happy that we finally made a sale.

205
00:12:16,810 --> 00:12:20,950
And why did you put your soul
into giving him a refund like that?

206
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:24,280
Even if our sales
take a hit right now,

207
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:27,050
that customer will come back
to our store...

208
00:12:27,050 --> 00:12:29,450
again and again in the future.

209
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:32,560
We showed him
that we did our best just for him.

210
00:12:33,090 --> 00:12:36,030
It would be nice
if everyone thought like you.

211
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:41,170
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

212
00:12:41,230 --> 00:12:43,870
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

213
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:45,840
(Incoming Call)

214
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,040
What is this?

215
00:12:54,180 --> 00:12:55,980
You finally answered.

216
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:59,280
If you didn't answer this time,
I was going to storm into the lobby.

217
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,950
We agreed never to contact
each other again.

218
00:13:03,690 --> 00:13:05,260
What are you doing right now?

219
00:13:06,190 --> 00:13:09,790
What are you doing?
You blocked my number.

220
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:12,760
Because we have no reason
to see each other anymore.

221
00:13:13,430 --> 00:13:14,430
Right?

222
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:17,970
We are still blood,
and I'm your elder.

223
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,840
After everything
I have done for you,

224
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:22,140
getting blocked
by my successful niece...

225
00:13:22,310 --> 00:13:24,010
really hurt my feelings.

226
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:26,510
Make sure you save this number.

227
00:13:27,010 --> 00:13:30,010
Who knows?
I might need to contact you again.

228
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:32,350
I gave you everything you asked for.

229
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:35,090
What else could you possibly
need to contact me about?

230
00:13:35,750 --> 00:13:38,220
Then you shouldn't have blocked me.

231
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:40,560
You treated me like a bug.

232
00:13:41,690 --> 00:13:43,330
Now that I have money,

233
00:13:44,090 --> 00:13:47,200
I suddenly have all this free time,
and I want to find her.

234
00:13:48,570 --> 00:13:50,230
Find who?

235
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,940
That child, Da Mi.

236
00:13:55,970 --> 00:13:58,310
Do you think I would bat an eye
at that?

237
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:01,550
I searched for her for years
and couldn't find her.

238
00:14:01,550 --> 00:14:03,150
She is no longer in this world.

239
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:04,250
And...

240
00:14:04,950 --> 00:14:06,350
why are you looking for her?

241
00:14:07,050 --> 00:14:08,390
What are you going to do
when you find her?

242
00:14:09,050 --> 00:14:10,050
Well,

243
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:12,690
three million dollars
isn't quite enough for me.

244
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:15,590
I suppose I'm still feeling hungry.

245
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:18,030
So I thought about it.

246
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:19,560
A cornucopia.

247
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:22,900
Da Mi will be
my endless source of wealth.

248
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:25,100
If I find that child,

249
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,540
I feel like she will be
a very useful tool for me someday.

250
00:14:30,610 --> 00:14:32,740
I'm a very deep thinker.

251
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,280
What do you think?

252
00:14:34,610 --> 00:14:37,110
If I find her,
it will be good for me,

253
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:39,920
but don't you think your life
will become very interesting too?

254
00:14:40,950 --> 00:14:42,720
Go ahead and do whatever you want.

255
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:45,120
I don't care.

256
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:52,430
Now that she has her money,

257
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:55,500
she must have absolutely
nothing better to do.

258
00:14:57,470 --> 00:14:59,040
She took three million dollars,

259
00:15:00,270 --> 00:15:02,510
and she dares to threaten me again?

260
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:06,680
She's not human.

261
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:09,450
She really isn't.

262
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:12,550
Hey. It's Mom.

263
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:14,750
Oh, are you busy?

264
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:19,360
It's a slow time for customers,
so I'm vacuuming...

265
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:21,830
and hanging the laundry. Why?

266
00:15:23,290 --> 00:15:26,200
Mom, about what you were going
to tell me yesterday.

267
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,270
What do you mean?

268
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:32,400
You asked me
how much money I had saved up.

269
00:15:33,170 --> 00:15:34,940
Oh, that.

270
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:38,140
You didn't just ask that
for no reason, did you?

271
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:42,850
I just asked.
Why are you worrying about it?

272
00:15:44,150 --> 00:15:45,850
Mom, why are you lying to me?

273
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,420
Why would I lie to you?

274
00:15:49,690 --> 00:15:50,690
Mom,

275
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:53,620
you want to pay off Dae Chi's debt.

276
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:56,130
That's why you asked me.

277
00:15:56,690 --> 00:15:59,430
Right? Tell me I'm wrong.

278
00:16:04,870 --> 00:16:05,870
I'm right.

279
00:16:06,670 --> 00:16:07,970
You do want to pay it for him.

280
00:16:09,270 --> 00:16:11,210
That's why you asked me.

281
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:13,910
Is a mother not allowed...

282
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:16,050
to ask her daughter a question?

283
00:16:19,150 --> 00:16:20,850
If anyone should be repaying her,

284
00:16:21,690 --> 00:16:23,050
shouldn't it be you?

285
00:16:24,050 --> 00:16:26,760
Hey, what are you talking about?

286
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:29,490
Yes, Mom...

287
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:33,330
raised the three of us
all by herself after Dad left.

288
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:36,000
So if anyone needs to repay
that debt of gratitude,

289
00:16:36,270 --> 00:16:38,400
it should be you.

290
00:16:41,510 --> 00:16:42,510
Da Mi.

291
00:16:43,470 --> 00:16:44,480
Sweetie.

292
00:16:45,180 --> 00:16:46,210
Hello?

293
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:48,110
No, Mom.

294
00:16:49,310 --> 00:16:51,850
We are mother and daughter,
so of course you can ask.

295
00:16:52,350 --> 00:16:53,950
We are mother and daughter.

296
00:16:54,750 --> 00:16:57,820
Anyway, you really want to help
Dae Chi out.

297
00:17:00,090 --> 00:17:01,290
I did,

298
00:17:02,390 --> 00:17:05,330
but you heard what Grandma
said this morning too.

299
00:17:06,530 --> 00:17:08,670
I don't have the money to help him,

300
00:17:09,270 --> 00:17:10,970
and if I get a loan
behind Grandma's back,

301
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:12,570
she will be furious.

302
00:17:15,840 --> 00:17:17,780
He has to figure it out himself.
What else can we do?

303
00:17:18,410 --> 00:17:20,680
At least he has a secure job.

304
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:24,680
But why did you cry yesterday?

305
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:28,790
Did you cry because I asked
how much money you have saved?

306
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:32,820
Or did Dae Chi do something...

307
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:37,130
Who said I was crying?
You're talking nonsense, Mom.

308
00:17:38,030 --> 00:17:39,460
I'm hanging up. I have to work now.

309
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,170
Okay.

310
00:17:41,530 --> 00:17:43,630
Come home early,
and watch out for cars.

311
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,810
Does Mom think I'm a child?

312
00:17:49,140 --> 00:17:50,540
She always tells me
to watch out for cars.

313
00:17:56,010 --> 00:17:57,110
(Connecting to Haedeul Bank)

314
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:59,880
(Future Savings: 218,870 dollars)

315
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:03,390
I felt like I could
lift the earth with this money,

316
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:07,460
but why does 200,000 dollars
look so small today?

317
00:18:08,730 --> 00:18:10,430
Seriously, 1,130,000 dollars?

318
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,230
Crazy jerk.

319
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:16,700
Even if he is drowning in debt,
how could he cut ties with me now?

320
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:18,140
And he calls himself my brother?

321
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:21,670
What a waste of a good education.

322
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:32,680
Excuse me, Team Leader.

323
00:18:33,220 --> 00:18:35,350
I think there is
a huge misunderstanding.

324
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:38,920
I swear I have absolutely nothing
to do with what you are suspecting.

325
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:43,760
Embezzlement?
That's completely absurd.

326
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:47,100
I haven't said anything yet.

327
00:18:48,570 --> 00:18:49,600
Right.

328
00:18:50,470 --> 00:18:53,240
You've been in constant contact
with Deputy Manager Kim Dong Seok.

329
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:54,370
Is that correct?

330
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,310
That's because Kim Pro...

331
00:18:56,670 --> 00:18:57,880
No...

332
00:18:58,010 --> 00:19:01,710
I had a specific reason
to contact Deputy Manager Kim.

333
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:03,110
What is that reason?

334
00:19:04,110 --> 00:19:06,780
I can't tell you right now,

335
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:09,790
but anyway, it's not
what you are misunderstanding.

336
00:19:17,730 --> 00:19:18,730
Even after seeing this?

337
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,270
(Manager Kang: Keep your promise.)

338
00:19:21,330 --> 00:19:22,530
(Deputy Manager Kim:
I will match the amount.)

339
00:19:25,070 --> 00:19:27,640
You were in charge of orders
for Uijeong Trading, Manager Kang?

340
00:19:29,270 --> 00:19:32,140
Yes. But is there a problem with...

341
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:33,610
Manager Kang Dae Chi.

342
00:19:33,780 --> 00:19:36,680
We have secured evidence that
you embezzled 1.2 million dollars...

343
00:19:37,580 --> 00:19:38,920
over the past three years...

344
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:41,150
through fake orders
and forged documents...

345
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:42,720
involving Uijeong Trading,
a shell company.

346
00:19:43,020 --> 00:19:45,490
Did you say 1,200,000 dollars?

347
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:49,490
I only placed the orders
under Deputy Manager Kim's orders.

348
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:52,230
I didn't even know Uijeong Trading
was a shell company.

349
00:19:52,330 --> 00:19:54,500
I only just found out now
because you said it was.

350
00:19:55,370 --> 00:19:57,630
Everyone who comes to the audit office
says the same thing,

351
00:19:57,770 --> 00:19:58,870
saying they didn't know.

352
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:02,340
Is there a manual going around?

353
00:20:02,670 --> 00:20:07,240
But when we thoroughly check
their bank accounts,

354
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:10,950
they are always holding onto
that embezzled money tightly.

355
00:20:11,680 --> 00:20:13,220
It's really not me.

356
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:14,620
This is so unfair.

357
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:16,920
Yes, I'm sure you feel it's unfair.

358
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:19,960
The information confirmed
by the audit team alone...

359
00:20:20,590 --> 00:20:22,390
is grounds
for immediate termination,

360
00:20:22,690 --> 00:20:24,930
but a disciplinary committee will be
held according to procedure.

361
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:28,730
A disciplinary committee?

362
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:31,940
Yes. As of this moment,
Manager Kang Dae Chi,

363
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:34,400
you are relieved of your duties
and suspended from work.

364
00:20:34,570 --> 00:20:36,770
Your company intranet account
will be blocked,

365
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:39,010
and your access to the company's
secure areas will be restricted.

366
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:40,940
No.

367
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,610
What is going on...

368
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:48,790
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

369
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:52,820
- Did you call for me, ma'am?
- Assistant Manager Kang.

370
00:20:53,390 --> 00:20:57,530
In a few days, we're meeting the CEO
of Summit Investment from the US.

371
00:20:57,530 --> 00:20:59,000
- You know this, right?
- Yes.

372
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:01,370
I'm aware that
it's an important meeting.

373
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,970
Since your English is excellent,
Assistant Manager Kang,

374
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:06,770
I would like you to accompany me
to this meeting.

375
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,240
Me?

376
00:21:09,570 --> 00:21:12,040
- Are you not up for it?
- Not at all.

377
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:13,440
It's an honor, ma'am.

378
00:21:14,210 --> 00:21:16,080
Should I also take charge
of the overall preparations?

379
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:17,180
Of course.

380
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:20,180
They said they will be staying
for 4 days and 3 nights,

381
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:23,190
so coordinate hotels, restaurants,
and other concierge services...

382
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:26,590
to ensure everything runs smoothly.

383
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:30,530
Since this meeting
was arranged so suddenly,

384
00:21:30,530 --> 00:21:35,470
it will be hectic,
but we must secure this investment.

385
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,840
It will be a good opportunity
for you as well.

386
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,040
Yes, I will get everything ready.

387
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:45,480
By the way.

388
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:49,110
Are you still going
to the fitness center?

389
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:50,750
Yes.

390
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:52,220
Thanks to you, I'm strengthening...

391
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:53,720
my body and mind
in a great environment.

392
00:21:54,250 --> 00:21:55,350
Thank you.

393
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:58,120
Then you must run into
our Do Yun as well?

394
00:21:58,320 --> 00:21:59,320
Pardon?

395
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:01,320
Yes.

396
00:22:01,390 --> 00:22:03,760
He's someone who strictly separates
his personal and work life.

397
00:22:04,390 --> 00:22:06,360
Even if you ran into him
at the fitness center,

398
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:07,600
he was probably aloof.

399
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:09,500
How do you know that so well?

400
00:22:10,430 --> 00:22:11,900
Because I raised him.

401
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:13,770
Because I'm his mom.

402
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:16,840
Try to make
a good impression on him.

403
00:22:17,470 --> 00:22:19,080
Don't give up after a few tries.

404
00:22:20,110 --> 00:22:22,910
You're a very charming woman,
Assistant Manager Kang.

405
00:22:25,620 --> 00:22:29,720
How should I prepare your outfit
for the meeting that day, ma'am?

406
00:22:30,550 --> 00:22:33,020
You don't need to worry about that.
I will take care of it myself.

407
00:22:34,290 --> 00:22:36,660
- You may leave.
- Yes.

408
00:22:44,030 --> 00:22:46,740
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

409
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:50,940
Da Mi.

410
00:22:51,070 --> 00:22:52,180
What do you think?

411
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:55,050
If I find her,
it will be good for me,

412
00:22:55,110 --> 00:22:57,710
but don't you think your life
will become very interesting too?

413
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:01,450
It will become interesting?

414
00:23:04,290 --> 00:23:06,320
Do you really think things will go
your way?

415
00:23:11,090 --> 00:23:13,830
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

416
00:23:19,340 --> 00:23:20,340
Yes, that's right.

417
00:23:20,470 --> 00:23:22,970
So you're saying
there were no tablets turned in...

418
00:23:22,970 --> 00:23:24,070
to the lost and found?

419
00:23:25,510 --> 00:23:26,840
Yes, I understand.

420
00:23:28,410 --> 00:23:30,550
- Da Mi. Let's go.
- Okay.

421
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:34,790
(K Department Store)

422
00:23:38,120 --> 00:23:39,290
- But Da Mi.
- Yes?

423
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:42,090
Isn't the tablet you lost
registered as a device?

424
00:23:42,560 --> 00:23:44,060
The location should show up
on the app.

425
00:23:44,530 --> 00:23:47,200
You're right.
Why did I forget about that?

426
00:23:48,300 --> 00:23:49,330
See you later.

427
00:23:49,830 --> 00:23:50,830
Good work today.

428
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:56,440
(Da Mi's Tablet)

429
00:23:56,870 --> 00:23:59,440
If it's 1.6km away,
it's a 25-minute walk?

430
00:24:04,050 --> 00:24:05,350
Ri Ja.

431
00:24:06,050 --> 00:24:07,620
Mona Ri Ja.

432
00:24:08,220 --> 00:24:11,050
You said you were taking a break,
so what are you doing?

433
00:24:11,120 --> 00:24:12,590
The customers are flooding in.

434
00:24:13,790 --> 00:24:17,390
I'm coming, Mrs. Choi.

435
00:24:17,390 --> 00:24:18,460
Gosh, my back.

436
00:24:19,630 --> 00:24:22,170
I told you to go to a clinic
or a Korean medicine doctor.

437
00:24:22,670 --> 00:24:24,170
What will you do
if it becomes chronic?

438
00:24:25,500 --> 00:24:28,610
Then you should raise my allowance.

439
00:24:30,410 --> 00:24:31,410
This is so hard.

440
00:24:48,530 --> 00:24:51,230
Mother, I have return...

441
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:53,660
Who is this?

442
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:58,900
I was right in the middle
of setting the mood.

443
00:25:04,770 --> 00:25:07,580
Mother, I have returned.

444
00:25:11,650 --> 00:25:12,680
Wait, what's this?

445
00:25:13,750 --> 00:25:16,120
No matter how busy he is,
he always answers my calls.

446
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:21,160
It's not a dream.

447
00:25:22,090 --> 00:25:23,390
I hoped it was a dream.

448
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:43,280
Why is the air so stuffy?

449
00:25:44,750 --> 00:25:46,380
Goodness, where is my head?

450
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:04,030
I wonder how the kids have grown up.

451
00:26:05,270 --> 00:26:08,100
But Jo Mi Mi,

452
00:26:09,110 --> 00:26:12,710
did she only eat one meal a day?
How is she still so slender?

453
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:17,010
She will be 60 soon, right?

454
00:26:18,250 --> 00:26:21,580
She still looks
like a cosmos flower.

455
00:26:23,420 --> 00:26:24,450
A sunflower.

456
00:26:24,820 --> 00:26:28,590
Yes, Mi Mi used to love
moss rose too, right?

457
00:26:29,190 --> 00:26:31,230
She said she wanted to plant
a bunch of those flowers...

458
00:26:31,430 --> 00:26:32,530
and grow them in the yard.

459
00:26:35,630 --> 00:26:40,300
Well, at least I planted my sons
before I left.

460
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:44,110
Goodness.

461
00:27:06,700 --> 00:27:08,800
- Excuse me.
- Yes.

462
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:10,900
Is there anything you need?

463
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:13,070
How many of these
do you have in stock?

464
00:27:13,170 --> 00:27:14,170
Just a moment.

465
00:27:17,010 --> 00:27:18,110
(Align in the square)

466
00:27:18,110 --> 00:27:19,310
(Searching database...)

467
00:27:20,110 --> 00:27:21,210
(Women's Cape Blouse,
Current Inventory: 3)

468
00:27:21,510 --> 00:27:23,410
There are three of each color.

469
00:27:24,610 --> 00:27:26,380
Could you tell me
where they were manufactured?

470
00:27:26,450 --> 00:27:28,520
Yes, I will check and let you know.

471
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:29,720
Okay.

472
00:27:38,860 --> 00:27:41,200
Just wait until I catch you.
I won't let you get away with this.

473
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:43,330
(Da Mi's Tablet)

474
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:07,590
(Mission: Mompossible)

475
00:28:07,790 --> 00:28:09,230
I knew it was strange
how the Uijeong Trading orders...

476
00:28:09,230 --> 00:28:10,890
were always given verbally.

477
00:28:11,760 --> 00:28:13,600
You really got played, Kang Dae Chi.

478
00:28:13,930 --> 00:28:17,500
How will you pay 600 dollars
for living expenses every month?

479
00:28:17,770 --> 00:28:19,140
Dad, why aren't you working?

480
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:21,910
I caught you, you thief.

481
00:28:22,140 --> 00:28:24,910
Be at Exit Three at Unjeong Station
by 2 p.m. tomorrow.

482
00:28:25,140 --> 00:28:27,280
If you are late,
we won't ever see each other again.

483
00:28:28,410 --> 00:28:30,410
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
